# Everything here goes THROUGH the gateway (5100). Start ProductService (5101) and OrderService (5102) first.
@Gateway = http://localhost:5100

### Gateway info (answered by the gateway itself)
GET {{Gateway}}/

### Gateway health (answered by the gateway itself)
GET {{Gateway}}/health

### Products -> forwarded to ProductService (5101)
GET {{Gateway}}/api/products
Accept: application/json

### One product -> forwarded to ProductService
GET {{Gateway}}/api/products/1
Accept: application/json

### Orders -> forwarded to OrderService (5102)
GET {{Gateway}}/api/orders
Accept: application/json

### Place an order -> OrderService, which itself calls ProductService directly (not through the gateway)
# @name createOrder
POST {{Gateway}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Gateway Test",
  "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### Cancel the order placed above (the Location header of the POST also points to the gateway)
DELETE {{Gateway}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### No route for this path (404 from the gateway)
GET {{Gateway}}/api/unknown

### Stop ProductService and run "One product" again: the gateway answers 502 Bad Gateway.
